LogTotal HOWTO

November 02, 2026
3 min read

LogTotal accepts three kinds of files: Windows event logs in EVTX, JSON (one event per line works best), and syslog-style text. Text and JSON uploads go through the sanitize step before analysis; EVTX files don’t yet. If your logs are in some other shape, there’s almost always a one-line command that converts them. The common ones are listed below.

LogTotal is SOC Prime’s free service for running detection logic against a log file without setting anything up: upload, sanitize, review. Getting the format right is the only part that can trip you up, so this page is the short version.

