Getting JSON right

One event per line is the safest shape. Many tools wrap events in arrays or envelopes. Flatten them before uploading:

You haveFlatten withA JSON array (gcloud, az, many APIs)jq -c ‘.[]’ in.json > out.jsonlCloudTrail log filesjq -c ‘.Records[]’ *.json > out.jsonlaws cloudtrail lookup-events outputjq -c ‘.Events[].CloudTrailEvent | fromjson’ in.json > out.jsonlCloudWatch Logs eventsjq -c ‘.events[].message | fromjson’ in.json > out.jsonlSplunk REST JSON exportjq -c ‘select(.result) | .result’ in.json > out.jsonl

Watch the encoding on Windows. Windows PowerShell 5.1 writes UTF-16 when you use > or Out-File without options. Add -Encoding utf8, as every PowerShell example in our guides does.

Keep the time zone. ISO 8601 timestamps with Z or an offset make findings line up with other sources. Classic syslog timestamps have no year and no zone; note the source’s time zone when you upload them.

Converting what LogTotal doesn’t read

You haveConvert withsystemd journal files (.journal)journalctl -D <dir> -o json –no-pager > out.jsonlA macOS .logarchivelog show –archive <file> –style json > out.json (on a Mac)EVTX, but you want the sanitize stepevtx_dump -o jsonl in.evtx > out.jsonlGzipped logszcat -f in.log.gz > out.log A spreadsheet or XML export from a SIEM’s web interfaceRe-export through the platform’s API or CLI; see

Size

split -l 200000 big.jsonl part_

For EVTX, filter while exporting with wevtutil /q

FAQ Does LogTotal keep my files?No. Uploads are analyzed and not retained.Will more formats be supported?Yes. We add formats regularly, and this page always lists what works today.

